<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Antonio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1718">1718</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as San Antonio de Béxar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">San Antonio is a city in south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> founded by the Spanish in 1718 as a mission and presidio on the San Antonio River. It became the chief settlement and from 1772 the capital of Spanish Texas, and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alamo-mission">Mission San Antonio de Valero</a>, the Alamo, was besieged in 1836 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas-revolution">Texas Revolution</a>. Mexican forces briefly occupied the town twice in 1842.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-antonio.jpg" alt="San Antonio" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jouaienttoi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:San_Antonio_Botanical_Garden_Overlook_View.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
